# Markie

Markdown pages that compile into fast, mostly-static websites, with tiny reactive islands only where the document asks for them.

<a class="btn primary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
<a class="btn" href="/reactive/">Try reactivity</a>
</section>

:note "Markie stays true to the original vision: zero JavaScript for static routes, a sub-5 KB target for reactive pages, .skin styling, includes instead of components, and a folder router."

## What to try

